<%# locals: subscription:

    What "Not working" or "Wrong address" means and what to do about it —
    nothing at all when the subscription is fine. Paired with
    `_status_pill`, and shared by the same two screens for the same reason. %>
<% if subscription.broken? %>
  <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-removed" data-testid="broken-reason">
    <%= subscription.broken_reason %> Prism tried
    <%= WebhookSubscription::MAX_CONSECUTIVE_FAILURES %> times and has stopped.
    Stop watching this repository and add it again to start over.
  </p>
<% elsif subscription.callback_stale? %>
  <%# Silent failure otherwise: GitHub keeps POSTing to an address nothing
      answers on, and because the request never reaches Prism there is
      nothing in any log here to find. %>
  <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-modified" data-testid="stale-reason">
    GitHub is still delivering to <code class="font-mono text-xs break-all"><%= subscription.callback_url %></code>,
    but Prism now answers on <code class="font-mono text-xs break-all"><%= Webhooks::CallbackUrl.current_or_nil %></code>.
    Nothing is arriving. Re-register to point the existing webhook at the new address —
    the secret and history are kept.
  </p>
<% elsif subscription.suspended? %>
  <%# Deliberately undramatic, and it asks for nothing. This state fixes
      itself: the next delivery retries, and signing in again replaces the
      token immediately. Telling people to "remove and re-add the repository"
      — which the old copy did, for a state that recovered on its own — sent
      them to do work that was never needed. %>
  <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-soft" data-testid="suspended-reason">
    <%= subscription.broken_reason %> Prism will try again on the next pull request
    in this repository, and signing in to Prism again fixes it straight away.
    If you have signed in since, it is already sorted.
  </p>
<% end %>
